    "meal_prep": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "m_sub": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Make it ahead",
            "subheading_size": "subtitle-md",
            "secondary_color": true
          }
        },
        "m_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The leeks are the part worth doing early",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Braised leeks keep for two days in the refrigerator and are arguably better on day two, once the shallot and the splash of cider have settled into them. Warm them gently while the poaching liquid comes up and you have turned a 45-minute dish into a 15-minute one.</p><p>Nothing else stretches. Poached fish goes firm and grainy on reheating, and the brown butter sauce splits once it cools and sets. Both are minutes of work at the end &mdash; make them when you are ready to eat.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_btn": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "Shop Steelhead, Sashimi Loin",
            "button_link": "/products/steelhead-sashimi-loin-12oz",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_size": "md",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "m_sub",
        "m_head",
        "m_text",
        "m_btn"
      ],
